    "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 22 at 9:49AM PDT until October 22 at 12:00PM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues. Canyon rock\nand mud slides possible.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Santa Barbara County in southwestern\nCalifornia...\n\n* WHEN...Until noon PDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nCanyon rock and mud slides possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 948 AM PDT, Doppler radar and rain gauges indicated heavy rain\ndue to scattered showers and thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area. Canyon\nrock and mud slides possible.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSanta Barbara, Montecito, Carpinteria, Summerland, Rincon Point,\nLa Conchita, Goleta, Mission Canyon and Hope Ranch.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.",
    "response": "Avoid",
